    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92272" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥέθος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εος</span>, τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>limb</i>, usu. in pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥέθεα</span>, <i>limbs</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχὴ δ᾽ ἐκ ῥεθέων πταμένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.856
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥεθέων ἐκ θυμὸν ἕληται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					22.68
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				23.39
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in sg.,
